## Task Management System Implementation Plan for thos

### Overview

This plan adds a hybrid task management system to the thos orchestration dashboard. Users can create personal tasks with priorities and statuses, and optionally delegate any task to a Claude agent for autonomous execution. The system integrates into the existing WebSocket-only architecture, reuses the SessionStore persistence pattern, and fits into the current two-column dashboard layout as a toggleable right-side panel.

---

### 1. Type Definitions -- `lib/types.ts`

Add the following types at the end of the file, after the existing UI state section.

**New types to add:**

```typescript
// ── Task system ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

export type TaskStatus = "todo" | "in-progress" | "done";
export type TaskPriority = "low" | "medium" | "high" | "urgent";

/** A user-created task, optionally linked to a Claude agent. */
export interface Task {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  description: string;
  status: TaskStatus;
  priority: TaskPriority;
  /** If delegated, the agentId of the spawned Claude agent. */
  agentId: string | null;
  createdAt: number;
  updatedAt: number;
}
```

**New Browser-to-Server message types:**

```typescript
/** Browser asks the server to create a new task. */
export interface BrowserCreateTask {
  type: "create_task";
  title: string;
  description: string;
  priority: TaskPriority;
}

/** Browser asks to update a task's fields. */
export interface BrowserUpdateTask {
  type: "update_task";
  taskId: string;
  updates: Partial<Pick<Task, "title" | "description" | "status" | "priority">>;
}

/** Browser asks to delete a task. */
export interface BrowserDeleteTask {
  type: "delete_task";
  taskId: string;
}

/** Browser asks to delegate a task to a new Claude agent. */
export interface BrowserDelegateTask {
  type: "delegate_task";
  taskId: string;
}
```

Add these four types to the `BrowserMessage` union:

```typescript
export type BrowserMessage =
  | BrowserSpawn
  | BrowserSendMessage
  | BrowserControlResponse
  | BrowserKillAgent
  | BrowserDeleteAgent
  | BrowserRenameAgent
  | BrowserClearHistory
  | BrowserCreateTask      // new
  | BrowserUpdateTask      // new
  | BrowserDeleteTask      // new
  | BrowserDelegateTask;   // new
```

**New Server-to-Browser message types:**

```typescript
/** Server sends the full task list to the browser (on connect and after changes). */
export interface ServerTaskList {
  type: "task_list";
  tasks: Task[];
}

/** Server confirms a task was updated. */
export interface ServerTaskUpdated {
  type: "task_updated";
  task: Task;
}

/** Server confirms a task was deleted. */
export interface ServerTaskDeleted {
  type: "task_deleted";
  taskId: string;
}
```

Add these to the `ServerMessage` union:

```typescript
export type ServerMessage =
  | ServerRelay
  | ServerStatus
  | ServerError
  | ServerAgentList
  | ServerSpawned
  | ServerMessageHistory
  | ServerCliDisconnected
  | ServerCliConnected
  | ServerHistoryCleared
  | ServerTaskList       // new
  | ServerTaskUpdated    // new
  | ServerTaskDeleted;   // new
```

---

### 2. Task Persistence -- New file: `server/task-store.ts`

This class mirrors `SessionStore` exactly in pattern. It stores all tasks in a single file `$TMPDIR/thos-tasks/tasks.json` rather than one file per task (tasks are lightweight, no streaming, so a single file is simpler).

```typescript
/**
 * File-based task persistence for the thos dashboard.
 *
 * Stores all tasks in a single JSON file at `$TMPDIR/thos-tasks/tasks.json`.
 * Uses the same debounced/sync write pattern as SessionStore.
 */

import { mkdirSync, writeFileSync, readFileSync, existsSync } from "fs";
import { join } from "path";
import { tmpdir } from "os";
import type { Task } from "../lib/types";

const TASK_DIR = join(tmpdir(), "thos-tasks");
const TASK_FILE = join(TASK_DIR, "tasks.json");

export class TaskStore {
  private debounceTimer: ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | null = null;

  constructor() {
    mkdirSync(TASK_DIR, { recursive: true });
  }

  /** Load all tasks from disk. Returns empty array if file missing. */
  loadAll(): Task[] {
    if (!existsSync(TASK_FILE)) return [];
    try {
      const raw = readFileSync(TASK_FILE, "utf-8");
      return JSON.parse(raw) as Task[];
    } catch (err) {
      console.error("[task-store] failed to load:", err);
      return [];
    }
  }

  /** Debounced write (150ms). */
  save(tasks: Task[]): void {
    if (this.debounceTimer) clearTimeout(this.debounceTimer);
    this.debounceTimer = setTimeout(() => {
      this.debounceTimer = null;
      this.writeFile(tasks);
    }, 150);
  }

  /** Immediate write for critical changes. */
  saveSync(tasks: Task[]): void {
    if (this.debounceTimer) {
      clearTimeout(this.debounceTimer);
      this.debounceTimer = null;
    }
    this.writeFile(tasks);
  }

  /** Flush pending writes (for graceful shutdown). */
  flush(tasks: Task[]): void {
    if (this.debounceTimer) {
      clearTimeout(this.debounceTimer);
      this.debounceTimer = null;
    }
    this.writeFile(tasks);
  }

  private writeFile(tasks: Task[]): void {
    try {
      writeFileSync(TASK_FILE, JSON.stringify(tasks, null, 2));
    } catch (err) {
      console.error("[task-store] failed to write:", err);
    }
  }
}
```

**Design rationale**: Tasks are not streamed like agent messages, so a single-file approach avoids filesystem churn. The debounced save is kept for consistency, and `saveSync` is used for create/update/delete operations since they are user-triggered (low frequency, high importance).

---

### 3. WebSocket Server -- Modify `server/ws.ts`

**Changes:**

**A. Import and instantiate TaskStore:**

At the top, alongside the SessionStore import, add:

```typescript
import { TaskStore } from "./task-store";
```

After `const store = new SessionStore();` add:

```typescript
const taskStore = new TaskStore();
```

**B. Add in-memory task state:**

After the `agents` Map and `browserSockets` Set, add:

```typescript
/** All tasks, keyed by task ID. */
const tasks = new Map<string, Task>();

// Restore tasks from disk on startup
function restoreTasks() {
  const persisted = taskStore.loadAll();
  for (const t of persisted) {
    tasks.set(t.id, t);
  }
  console.log(`[restore] loaded ${persisted.length} tasks from disk`);
}
restoreTasks();
```

**C. Add task helper functions:**

```typescript
/** Build the full task list for the browser. */
function buildTaskList(): Task[] {
  return Array.from(tasks.values()).sort((a, b) => b.createdAt - a.createdAt);
}

/** Send the full task list to all browsers. */
function broadcastTaskList() {
  sendToBrowser({ type: "task_list", tasks: buildTaskList() });
}

/** Persist all tasks to disk (sync). */
function persistTasks() {
  taskStore.saveSync(Array.from(tasks.values()));
}
```

**D. Handle new browser message types in `handleBrowserMessage`:**

Add four new cases to the `switch (msg.type)` block:

```typescript
case "create_task": {
  const taskId = randomBytes(4).toString("hex");
  const task: Task = {
    id: taskId,
    title: msg.title,
    description: msg.description,
    status: "todo",
    priority: msg.priority,
    agentId: null,
    createdAt: Date.now(),
    updatedAt: Date.now(),
  };
  tasks.set(taskId, task);
  persistTasks();
  broadcastTaskList();
  break;
}

case "update_task": {
  const task = tasks.get(msg.taskId);
  if (!task) break;
  Object.assign(task, msg.updates, { updatedAt: Date.now() });
  persistTasks();
  sendToBrowser({ type: "task_updated", task });
  broadcastTaskList();
  break;
}

case "delete_task": {
  tasks.delete(msg.taskId);
  persistTasks();
  sendToBrowser({ type: "task_deleted", taskId: msg.taskId });
  broadcastTaskList();
  break;
}

case "delegate_task": {
  const task = tasks.get(msg.taskId);
  if (!task) break;
  // Compose a prompt from the task
  const prompt = `Task: ${task.title}\n\n${task.description}`;
  const agentId = spawnClaude(prompt);
  task.agentId = agentId;
  task.status = "in-progress";
  task.updatedAt = Date.now();
  persistTasks();
  broadcastTaskList();
  break;
}
```

**E. Auto-update task status when a linked agent finishes:**

In the `handleClaudeMessage` function, after the `result` status handling block (`else if (msg.type === "result")`), add logic to update the linked task:

```typescript
// Auto-complete tasks linked to this agent
if (msg.type === "result") {
  const result = msg as ClaudeResult;
  for (const task of tasks.values()) {
    if (task.agentId === agentId) {
      task.status = result.is_error ? "todo" : "done";
      task.updatedAt = Date.now();
      persistTasks();
      broadcastTaskList();
      break;
    }
  }
}
```

**F. Send task list on browser connect:**

In `sendFullStateToSocket`, after sending the agent list and message histories, add:

```typescript
// 3. Task list
ws.send(JSON.stringify({ type: "task_list", tasks: buildTaskList() }));
```

**G. Update graceful shutdown:**

In the `shutdown` function, before `process.exit(0)`, add:

```typescript
taskStore.flush(Array.from(tasks.values()));
console.log(`[ws server] saved ${tasks.size} tasks to disk`);
```

---

### 4. WebSocket Client Hook -- Modify `hooks/use-websocket.ts`

**Changes:**

**A. Import the new `Task` type:**

Add `Task` to the import from `@/lib/types`.

**B. Add task state:**

After the existing `useState` calls for agents/agentOrder/activeAgentId, add:

```typescript
const [tasks, setTasks] = useState<Task[]>([]);
```

**C. Handle new server messages in `ws.onmessage`:**

Add three new handlers before the existing `agent_list` handler:

```typescript
// ── task_list: full task list from server ──
if (data.type === "task_list") {
  setTasks((data as ServerTaskList).tasks);
  return;
}

// ── task_updated: single task changed ──
if (data.type === "task_updated") {
  const updated = (data as ServerTaskUpdated).task;
  setTasks((prev) => prev.map((t) => (t.id === updated.id ? updated : t)));
  return;
}

// ── task_deleted: remove task ──
if (data.type === "task_deleted") {
  const deletedId = (data as ServerTaskDeleted).taskId;
  setTasks((prev) => prev.filter((t) => t.id !== deletedId));
  return;
}
```

**D. Add task action callbacks:**

After the existing `clearHistory` callback, add:

```typescript
const createTask = useCallback(
  (title: string, description: string, priority: TaskPriority) => {
    send({ type: "create_task", title, description, priority });
  },
  [send]
);

const updateTask = useCallback(
  (taskId: string, updates: Partial<Pick<Task, "title" | "description" | "status" | "priority">>) => {
    send({ type: "update_task", taskId, updates });
  },
  [send]
);

const deleteTask = useCallback(
  (taskId: string) => {
    send({ type: "delete_task", taskId });
  },
  [send]
);

const delegateTask = useCallback(
  (taskId: string) => {
    send({ type: "delegate_task", taskId });
  },
  [send]
);
```

**E. Return new values:**

Add to the return object:

```typescript
return {
  // ...existing...
  tasks,
  createTask,
  updateTask,
  deleteTask,
  delegateTask,
};
```

---

### 5. New UI Components

#### 5a. Task Card -- `components/dashboard/task-card.tsx`

A single task displayed as a compact card. Shows title, priority badge, status badge, optional linked agent indicator, and action buttons (edit, delegate, delete). Clicking the linked agent indicator should navigate to that agent in the chat view.

```
+--------------------------------------------------+
| [priority badge]  Task Title           [...menu] |
| Description text (truncated to 2 lines)          |
| [status badge]  [agent link or delegate button]  |
+--------------------------------------------------+
```

Key implementation details:
- Priority badges use color coding: `urgent` = red, `high` = orange, `medium` = yellow/amber, `low` = muted gray
- Status badges: `todo` = outline, `in-progress` = blue, `done` = green strikethrough on title
- When `agentId` is set, show a small link "View agent" that calls `onSelectAgent(agentId)`
- Use the existing `cn()` utility and Tailwind classes matching the dark-first theme
- Context menu (matching AgentSidebar's pattern) with: Edit, Delegate to Agent, Delete

Props interface:
```typescript
interface TaskCardProps {
  task: Task;
  onUpdate: (taskId: string, updates: Partial<Pick<Task, "title" | "description" | "status" | "priority">>) => void;
  onDelete: (taskId: string) => void;
  onDelegate: (taskId: string) => void;
  onSelectAgent: (agentId: string) => void;
}
```

#### 5b. Task Create Form -- `components/dashboard/task-create-form.tsx`

A compact inline form at the top of the task panel. Title input, description textarea, priority select, and a "Create" button. Follows the same form style as the chat input bar.

Props:
```typescript
interface TaskCreateFormProps {
  onCreate: (title: string, description: string, priority: TaskPriority) => void;
}
```

#### 5c. Task Panel -- `components/dashboard/task-panel.tsx`

The main container component. Shows the create form at top, then a scrollable list of TaskCards grouped by status: "In Progress" first, then "Todo", then "Done" (collapsed by default).

Props:
```typescript
interface TaskPanelProps {
  tasks: Task[];
  onCreateTask: (title: string, description: string, priority: TaskPriority) => void;
  onUpdateTask: (taskId: string, updates: Partial<Pick<Task, "title" | "description" | "status" | "priority">>) => void;
  onDeleteTask: (taskId: string) => void;
  onDelegateTask: (taskId: string) => void;
  onSelectAgent: (agentId: string) => void;
}
```

Layout:
```
+------------------------------+
| TASKS                   [+]  |  <- header with create toggle
+------------------------------+
| [Create form, collapsible]   |
+------------------------------+
| IN PROGRESS                  |
| [TaskCard]                   |
| [TaskCard]                   |
+------------------------------+
| TODO                         |
| [TaskCard]                   |
+------------------------------+
| DONE (3)               [v]   |  <- collapsible
| [TaskCard - muted]           |
+------------------------------+
```

Use Lucide icons: `ListTodo` for the panel header, `Plus` for create, `Play` for delegate, `Trash2` for delete, `ExternalLink` for agent link.

---

### 6. Dashboard Layout -- Modify `app/dashboard/page.tsx`

**Changes:**

Add a toggleable task panel as a right-side column. The layout becomes: Sidebar (w-56) | Chat (flex-1) | TaskPanel (w-80, conditional).

**A. Destructure new values from `useWebSocket`:**

```typescript
const {
  // ...existing...
  tasks,
  createTask,
  updateTask,
  deleteTask,
  delegateTask,
} = useWebSocket();
```

**B. Add panel toggle state:**

```typescript
const [showTasks, setShowTasks] = useState(false);
```

**C. Update the JSX layout:**

```tsx
<div className="flex h-dvh">
  <AgentSidebar ... />
  <div className="flex flex-1 flex-col">
    <Chat ... />
  </div>
  {showTasks && (
    <div className="w-80 border-l flex flex-col">
      <TaskPanel
        tasks={tasks}
        onCreateTask={createTask}
        onUpdateTask={updateTask}
        onDeleteTask={deleteTask}
